// operations.proto — DashCenter northbound operational lifecycle API.
//
// This service models the operational primitives that bracket a DPU's
// participation in the fleet: cordon (stop scheduling new placements),
// uncordon (resume), and drain (rehome existing workloads off the DPU
// through a controlled sequence of ENI live migrations).
//
// Workflow
// --------
// A typical maintenance window looks like:
//
//   1. CordonDpu   — DPU stops accepting NEW ENI placements.
//   2. DrainDpu    — dashd plans + executes ENI migrations off the DPU
//                    (uses MigrationService internally; see migration.proto).
//                    Returns a server stream of DrainProgress.
//   3. (operator performs the physical maintenance)
//   4. UncordonDpu — DPU is eligible for new placements again.
//
// Cordon is idempotent. Drain is idempotent IF a drain is already in
// progress (returns the in-flight stream); otherwise it kicks off a new one.
//
// Safety
// ------
// DrainDpu refuses to start if it cannot find candidate target DPUs with
// sufficient capacity and matching capabilities for every ENI being rehomed.
// The pre-flight result is surfaced in the first DrainProgress message with
// phase = DRAIN_PHASE_PLANNING; clients should not assume success until
// phase = DRAIN_PHASE_COMPLETE.

